Title: Trim resident git.md/workflow.md duplicates into /merge and /gaze
Created: 2026-09-10
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-10T14:23Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

`rules/git.md` and `rules/workflow.md` are fully resident (no `paths:`
frontmatter) — loaded in every session of every project (`rules/README.md`).
Several of their bullets are recovery procedures for a specific moment
(a merge, a `/gaze` invocation) that already live, in full or in near-full
duplicate, inside the skill that owns that moment. Paying their prose in
every session that will never run `/merge` or `/gaze` is the same waste
`test_branch_cleanup_recipes.py` already ratchets against for the
`§ Branch cleanup` section (moved to `/roar` step 10, 2026-09-09).

## Actions taken

- `rules/git.md` § Merging: trimmed 7 bullets to short pointers; ported
  substance to `skills/merge/SKILL.md` (`## Before merging`, `## Merge
  conflict recovery`) and `skills/gaze/SKILL.md` (`## Invariants`,
  branch-currency prerequisite).
- `rules/workflow.md` § Worktree paths: trimmed the memory carve-out
  corollary to a one-line pointer at `/roar` step 6, which already carries
  the fuller procedure (including the background-session case that
  `workflow.md` never had).
- Added `tests/test_git_md_merging_delegates.py`, a string-match ratchet
  mirroring `test_branch_cleanup_recipes.py`: proves the content moved,
  not merely duplicated.

## Explicitly descoped (found not worth the risk)

- `rules/git.md` § Repo layout "Prose workpackages" bullet: cited by name
  from `skills/gaze/SKILL.md`, `skills/hunt/SKILL.md`, `rules/workflow.md`,
  and pinned by `tests/test_gaze_prose_routing.py`. The ~150-word saving
  did not justify breaking a tested citation chain tied to a real incident
  (ticket 0550). Left untouched.
- "Reviewers are decorrelated from the coder" (`rules/workflow.md`
  § Delegation): `/gaze`'s own SKILL.md already cites this bullet as its
  source (`rules/workflow.md § Delegation`) — it is the canonical origin,
  not a duplicate. Extracting it would invert the citation. Left untouched.
- Child-ticket-split-before-work paragraph (`rules/workflow.md` § Ticket
  discipline): fires at planning time, before any specific skill is
  invoked — no clean skill-shaped home. Left untouched.

## Verification

- `make check-fast` and `make lint` (adherence tier) both green except one
  pre-existing, unrelated failure (`test_real_scripts_dir_is_agnostic`,
  origin/main commits `b49f01a`/`625932a`, files this ticket never touched).
- `./scripts/check-agnostic.sh skills` and `rules` both exit 0.
- Resident savings, measured via `wc -c` before/after: `rules/git.md`
  10086 → 8994 chars (−1092); `rules/workflow.md` 14155 → 13840 chars
  (−315). Total ≈ 1.4 kB (~500 tokens at the census's 2.8 chars/token) off
  every session's resident budget.

## Exit criteria

- [x] `rules/git.md` § Merging bullets point at `/merge`/`/gaze` instead of
      inlining recovery procedures already owned there.
- [x] `rules/workflow.md` memory-carve-out corollary points at `/roar`
      step 6 instead of duplicating it.
- [x] `tests/test_git_md_merging_delegates.py` proves delegation, not mere
      duplication.
- [x] `make check-fast` and `make lint` pass (module pre-existing failure
      excepted).
- [x] `./scripts/check-agnostic.sh skills rules` both exit 0.
